The image is labeled "LT LAT", indicating a left lateral chest X-ray. In a standard left lateral view, the patient's left side is against the detector (closer to the viewer in some conventions, but typically the spine is posterior and sternum anterior). However, determining "right" vs "left" lung opacity on a single lateral view without a PA/AP reference can be challenging due to superimposition.

Let's use `chest_xray_expert` to get a specialized interpretation of this lateral view to see if it identifies sidedness or specific opacities.

